192 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 522 0 R
/E (Determine whether any subset of the seven patterns functions as a reliable, computationally cheap signal for register classification, that is, whether a pattern's presence or frequency alone can distinguish formal from informal Hindi without requiring a trained classifier. A pattern qualifies as a strong register marker if it shows high distributional divergence between corpora and high regex F1 in at least one register, making it actionable without a neural pipeline. This finding would have practical implications for low-resource or real-time NLP applications on Hindi text.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
